{"id":"e19d778e-ab0b-4545-918e-934960b760ae","object":"chat.completion","created":1784825837,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    nodes = payload['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(payload['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {node['id']: node for node in nodes}\\n    root = next(n for n in nodes if n['parent'] is None)\\n    \\n    # Build children mapping\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            children[p].append(n['id'])\\n    \\n    # Identify removable nodes (excluding root)\\n    removable = [n['id'] for n in nodes if n['removable']]\\n    \\n    # Precompute ancestors for each node\\n    def get_ancestors(node_id):\\n        anc = set()\\n        cur = node_id\\n        while cur is not None:\\n            anc.add(cur)\\n            cur = node_map[cur]['parent']\\n        return anc\\n    \\n    ancestor_cache = {}\\n    for nid in nodes:\\n        ancestor_cache[nid['id']] = get_ancestors(nid['id'])\\n    \\n    # Non-removable nodes must be kept\\n    forced_non_removable = {n['id'] for n in nodes if not n['removable']}\\n    \\n    best_set = None\\n    best_utility = -1\\n    \\n    # Iterate over all subsets of removable nodes\\n    m = len(removable)\\n    for mask in range(1 << m):\\n        selected = set()\\n        for i in range(m):\\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\\n                selected.add(removable[i])\\n        # Compute kept set: forced non-removable + ancestors of selected\\n        kept = set(forced_non_removable)\\n        for nid in selected:\\n            kept.update(ancestor_cache[nid])\\n        # Ensure kept set is ancestor-closed (already ensured by ancestors)\\n        # Check connectivity: all kept nodes have parent in kept or are root\\n        # (Ancestor closure guarantees this)\\n        # Check coverage of required symbols\\n        symbols_in_kept = {node_map[nid]['symbol'] for nid in kept}\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_in_kept):\\n            continue\\n        # Compute utility\\n        utility = sum(node_map[nid]['utility'] for nid in kept)\\n        if utility > best_utility:\\n            best_utility = utility\\n            best_set = kept\\n    \\n    if best_set is None:\\n        # Fallback: keep all nodes (should not happen if problem is well-formed)\\n        best_set = {n['id'] for n in nodes}\\n    \\n    return {'kept_ids': list(best_set)}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce Python source code for `solve(case)` that takes a case with nodes and required_symbols. The task is \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\" from registered procedure SE-PE-01. The objective: Reduce a parse tree (nodes with parent references, depth, symbol, removable flag, utility) while preserving required symbols. We need to return something? The prompt says \"Return one JSON object with exactly one key, `implementation`. Its value must be Python source defining `solve(case)`. The function must return a JSON-serializable object, must not mutate `case`, and may use only the Python standard library.\"\n\nThe fixture shows cases with nodes and required_symbols. Likely we need to compute a reduced tree (subset of nodes) that still contains required symbols and is valid (i.e., each node's parent is present unless it's root, and perhaps the tree structure is preserved). Also \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\" suggests we can remove nodes that are removable, but we must keep nodes that are not removable? Also note \"utility\" values - might be used to choose which nodes to keep to maximize total utility? Possibly the objective is to maximize sum of utilities of kept nodes while satisfying constraints: include all required_symbols (i.e., nodes with those symbols, but there may be multiple nodes with same symbol? The fixture has m